-- title:
--   Two degeneracy maps generate the tower field
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N \neq 0$ and primes $q \neq q'$ with $q \nmid N$, $q' \nmid N$, and a natural number $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$. Let $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and a height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ is one where $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$; and let $\Lambda \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule that is an order maximal among the orders containing it. Let $\bar{F}$ be a field, a curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (principal divisors, finite residue extensions, and $\Omega_{\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ free of rank one) and essentially of finite type over it. Let $\pi_X : X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ be a morphism of schemes, $\bar{s}$ a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$, and `pt` a rule attaching, to each commutative ring $S$, each $S$-point $s$ of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ and each fake elliptic curve over $S$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, a point of $X$ over $s$; assume `pt` takes isomorphic fake elliptic curves to the same point (`pt_iso`), and that over an algebraically closed field equal values of `pt` force an isomorphism of fake elliptic curves (`pt_injective`). Let $\mathfrak{M}$ be a curve model of $\bar{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$ an isomorphism from $\mathfrak{M}.C$ to the pullback of $\pi_X$ along $\bar{s}$ whose composite with the second projection is $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{toBase}$, let `gal` and `galT` be homomorphisms from $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to semilinear automorphisms of $\bar{F}$, resp. of the tower fields, $W$ and $WT$ pairs of semilinear automorphisms, and $\mathbb{T}$ a tower datum consisting of curve fields $F_\ell$ for primes $\ell \neq q, q'$ together with finite integral $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra maps $\varphi_\alpha$ from $\bar{F}$. Given a witness `tw` of the predicate `ModuliTowerWitnessD` for these data, the conclusion is that for every prime $\ell \neq q, q'$ the subfield of $F_\ell$ generated by the union of the images of $\mathbb{T}.\varphi(\ell,0)$ and $\mathbb{T}.\varphi(\ell,1)$ is all of $F_\ell$.
--
--   The assertion is that the two degeneracy embeddings $\bar F \to F_\ell$ of the Shimura-curve Hecke tower attached to the indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q, q'$ jointly generate the upper field, i.e. that the correspondence $Y_\ell \to X \times X$, $(E,K) \mapsto (E, E/K)$, is birational onto its image. It supplies the generation hypothesis used in the uniqueness statements for the tower, and is cited in the extraction of descent data for the Čerednik–Drinfel'd comparison.
